Package: kubeos-kubernetes
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, kubelet (= 1.37.2-1.1), kubeadm (= 1.37.2-1.1), kubectl (= 1.37.2-1.1), kubernetes-cni (= 1.9.1-1.1)
Description: KubeOS: the pinned Kubernetes version a node runs
 Names the exact Kubernetes release a KubeOS node uses, and is what makes "which
 Kubernetes does this KubeOS run?" answerable with one command:
 .
     dpkg-query -W kubeos-kubernetes
 .
 kubelet, kubeadm, kubectl and kubernetes-cni are the upstream debs, copied into the
 KubeOS archive byte for byte. They are not rebuilt and not re-versioned, so they behave
 exactly like the upstream release - but they are only reachable from repo.kubeos.in, so
 `apt upgrade` can never move a node to a Kubernetes version KubeOS has not vetted. The
 upstream pkgs.k8s.io repository is not configured on a KubeOS node.
 .
 Upgrading a cluster is therefore a KubeOS decision, taken by publishing a new version of
 this package together with the matching debs (see PINNED and bin/mirror.sh).
